<section class="w3-process" id="inspection-process" aria-labelledby="w3-process-title">
  <div class="w3-process-inner">
    <header class="w3-process-heading">
      <p class="w3-process-kicker">WHAT TO EXPECT</p>
      <h2 id="w3-process-title">What happens during<br /><em>a leak inspection?</em></h2>
      <p>The checks depend on the signs and the plumbing at your property. The visit starts with what you’ve noticed and ends with an explanation of the findings.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="w3-process-steps">
      <li class="w3-process-step">
        <span class="w3-step-number">01</span>
        <div><h3>Show us the signs</h3><p>Point out where you noticed moisture, heard water, or saw a change in your bill.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li class="w3-process-step">
        <span class="w3-step-number">02</span>
        <div><h3>We check the likely area</h3><p>The technician reviews accessible areas and chooses checks based on the symptoms and plumbing.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li class="w3-process-step">
        <span class="w3-step-number">03</span>
        <div><h3>We explain what we found</h3><p>You’ll hear what was checked, what the evidence suggests, and what remains uncertain.</p></div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

